  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/amphiliidae/belonoglanis_tenuis.htm",
      "html": "<p>Members of this genus are long and slim and remind one of the \"whiptail\" species of South America. The specific name tenuis means slender or thin. Family: Amphiliidae. Size: 16 cm. Temperature: 24–28°C. pH: 6.2–7.2.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/amphiliidae/belonoglanis_tenuis.htm",
      "html": "<p>Not often imported. B. tenuis is more slender than other members of this genus and has a longer snout.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/amphiliidae/belonoglanis_tenuis.htm",
      "html": "<p>Africa: Congo River basin. Type locality: Ubangi à Banzyville.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/amphiliidae/belonoglanis_tenuis.htm",
      "html": "<p>Members of this genus are found at the margins of swift-flowing streams.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/amphiliidae/belonoglanis_tenuis.htm",
      "html": "<p>This genus prefers water with a bit of movement. Sand substrate with algae-covered rocks if possible.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/amphiliidae/belonoglanis_tenuis.htm",
      "html": "<p>Algae, vegetable foods such as peas, frozen mosquito larvae and tablet food.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/amphiliidae/belonoglanis_tenuis.htm",
      "html": "<p>IUCN Red List: the species is widespread or without major threats throughout the Central Africa assessment region and is assessed as Least Concern, but needs updating (IUCN 2010).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "references",
      "source": "scotcat",
